        { cardNumber: "0071", event: "T4_EVERY_LEASH_BREAKS",
          disagreement: "Bumper counts three pups out over her back and answers nobody; Backfire tells the wagon night with the fourth seat already empty before the catchers backed in -- the pup ran, and 'taken' is just easier to carry than 'left.' Bolt Corgi's telling is the one with hope in it, which is exactly why the block trusts it least: FOUR out, the smallest over the far fence on the old man's own back, and whatever rode away in the wagon was not theirs. But the far fence was Backfire's watch, and Backfire's telling requires the fence to have stayed empty, and a father's forgiveness requires it not to have -- so one of those two dogs is protecting the other with his version, and the sealed report at THE KENNEL knows which, and The Tracker greets them both the same gentle way, which proves nothing, which is precisely the old Bloodhound's point." }
